From 82bb5858c0b870185f72eea043b8ffd7c16d42eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:26:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stock: prefer wired backhaul and recover on link loss

DSA ports use their conduit as iflink, so treating iflink != ifindex as
virtual excludes the LAN ports from automatic wired backhaul discovery.
Recognize the kernel DSA device type and restart backhaul selection when
the selected wired port loses its link. Isolate standby STAs from the LAN
bridge before wired onboarding to prevent a parallel forwarding loop.

Keep normal discovery replies in the Agent's M1/M2 flow. Only use runtime
probes from the enrolled controller to promote a wireless uplink, and do
not replace a selected wired backhaul with standby STA traffic. Reply to
Ethernet discovery through the bridge: raw DSA port unicast TX can report
success without reaching the peer. Keep the wired backhaul station when
its Ethernet port shares the Agent's AL MAC. Disambiguate wired parents
from radio BSSIDs that collide with the synthetic Ethernet switch MAC.
Preserve enrolled Agent parents when answering runtime discovery probes.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
